  "construction_notes": [
    {
      "text": "Five-story building with a 21-car ground-level garage; replaced an office building and a six-unit apartment building",
      "src": [
        "SRC-000621"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "33 affordable units; the city also lists one manager's unit.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001256"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "CTCAC CA-24-085: Cherry Street Commons, located at 1244 Cherry Street in San Carlos, requested and is being recommended for a reservation of $2,085,934 in annual federal tax credits to finance the new construction of 32 units of housing serving families with rents affordable to households earning 30%-60% of area median income (AMI).",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001647"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Eden Housing project page lists the property as \"Now Accepting Applications\"; general contractor Echelcon, Inc.; 21 car spaces plus 2 accessible, 20 long-term bike and 8 scooter spaces; all-electric with rooftop PV.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-003653"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Leasing site (2026 CTCAC limits): maximum rents 1BR/2BR/3BR of $1,068/$1,263/$1,439 at 30% AMI, $1,856/$2,208/$2,531 at 50% AMI, and $2,150/$2,681/$3,078 at 60% AMI. Leasing contact 1244cherry@hiphousing.org.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-003655"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The Almanac (May 9, 2025): the city's former Redevelopment Agency envisioned the project in 2010; San Carlos is contributing $12.8 million from its Affordable Housing Fund.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-003654"
      ]
    }
  ],
